<title>SOUTH AFRICA: King Food interim shr dips.</title>
<headline>King Food interim shr dips.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended August 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     6.9	   vs  11.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.06	  vs   5.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   3.85	  vs   7.27</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.79	  vs   1.85</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.38	  vs   0.44 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover		 20.99	  vs  59.48</p>
<p>Full name: King Food Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said that in line with its stated policy, the group would pay about 33 percent of its distributable earnings to shareholders in the form of a single dividend.</p>
<p>The first dividend would be declared in May 1997 and paid in June 1997.</p>
<p>The group said it was poised for growth and should experience increased profitability and better trading margins as the number of franchised outlets increased. King Food said it continued to seek acquisitions to expand and complement its core business.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
